  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a tree of NNN nodes, and 222 arrays of size NNN - AAA and BBB.\n\nYou would like to ensure that Ai≠BiA_i \\neq B_iAi​=Bi​ for every 1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N.\n\nTo achieve this, you can perform the following operation **exactly once**:\n\n\nPick a subset S={X1,X2,…,X∣S∣}S = \\{X_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_{|S|}\\}S={X1​,X2​,…,X∣S∣​} of the nodes, such that the subgraph induced by SSS is **connected**.\n\nIn other words, if x,y∈Sx, y \\in Sx,y∈S, then every vertex on the (unique) path connecting xxx and yyy should also belong to SSS.\n\n\nThen, rearrange the values AX1,AX2,…,AX∣S∣A_{X_1}, A_{X_2}, \\ldots, A_{X_{|S|}}AX1​​,AX2​​,…,AX∣S∣​​ among positions X1,X2,…,X∣S∣X_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_{|S|}X1​,X2​,…,X∣S∣​, however you like.\nFind the **minimum** size of the subset SSS, and the number of ways to choose a minimum-sized subset SSS, such that it is possible to rearrange and meet the condition.\n\nSince the number of ways may be large, output it modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.\n\n**Note:**\n\n\nChoosing the empty subset is allowed. You can assume there exists exactly one way to choose an empty subset.\nThere may not exist any valid subset you can pick. In that case, output −1−1-1 -1−1−1.\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of input contains NNN - the size of the tree\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nThe third line contains NNN space-separated integers - B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​.\nThe next N−1N - 1N−1 lines contain 222 space-separated integers each, uuu and vvv, denoting an edge between uuu and vvv in the tree.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line 222 space-separated integers: first the minimum possible size of SSS, and second the number of ways to choose a minimum-sized SSS modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.\n\n\nIn case no valid subset exists, output −1−1-1 -1−1−1.",
